Now the headset (producer) will receive the `end` message. But looking at the headset's message handler — `end` is handled in `onMessage` at line 172:

```js
} else if (msg.type === "end") {
    player.stop?.();
    setCaption("Session ended.");
    setStatus("");
    voice?.close();
    voice = null;
}
```

This handles receiving an end message from the server. But wait — the headset is the producer, and the server sends this `end` message directly to the producer's WebSocket. The headset's voice.js `liveVoice` will parse it and call `onMessage({type:"end"})`. The headset's `onMessage` handler will then stop playback and show "Session ended." — but it won't exit AR or trigger the End button's cleanup.

Let me also make the headset handle incoming `end` messages more fully — exit AR session too:

